    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d71">

                <pb facs="0240" n="170" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg170"/>

                <head>No. 71.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Young
                        to Mr. Frelinghuysen</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1882-12-18"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 18, 1882</date>.
                        (Received February 23, 1883.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 78.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose for the information of the
                    Department a copy of a proclamation attributed to the King of Corea. This
                    document first appeared in a Japanese native journal, and afterwards in an
                    English Shanghai paper. The Department may have received it from the legation at
                    Tokio with such information, not attainable here, as will enable you to judge of
                    its authority, and if authentic, of its value as an impression of Corean
                    sentiment towards foreigners.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JNO. RUSSELL YOUNG.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d71-a1.xml" xpointer="d71-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
